 "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pgsty/mc/tarball/RELEASE.2026-09-13T00-00-00Z",
 "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pgsty/mc/zipball/RELEASE.2026-09-13T00-00-00Z",
 "body": "SILO mcli release `20260913000000`, packaged as `20260913000000.0.0` for Linux, macOS and Windows.\n\n### Fixes since the previous release\n\n- Preserve mirror targets when historical source versions are deleted.\n- Never turn an administrative restart dry run into a real restart; keep restart output reliable when stdout is not a terminal.\n- Return transfer and SQL per-object failures as unsuccessful commands without misreporting them as usage errors.\n- Preserve explicit checksums for empty uploads, honor pipe JSON/quiet flags, and accept on/off and enabled/disabled values in MC boolean environment variables.\n- Keep CLI JSON output and cross-platform functional-test behavior consistent.\n- Include silo-pkg policy fixes that preserve distinct Deny/NotResource clauses and string-condition values, and bound wildcard matching. Previously lost stored policy clauses still need to be restored from the original policy source.\n\n### Coordinated dependencies\n\nUse released `github.com/pgsty/silo-pkg/v3 v3.14.0` directly and upstream minio-go commit `60bd07042d49`, including streaming Content-Type signing, RDMA TLS trust, listing checksums and restore-status fixes. Refresh the Go official x/* dependencies and the UBI certificate image, retain Go 1.27.1, and run govulncheck 1.8.0. The go-systemd 22.6.0 replacement remains the documented NetBSD build compatibility exception.\n\nThe package's password policy behavior has changed: `admin:ChangeMyPassword` and `admin:CreateUser` are separate capabilities. Policies that must preserve the previous combined restriction should deny both actions with the same scope and conditions. Use matching SILO Server and Console versions; see [the migration guide](https://github.com/pgsty/silo/blob/420340bc142b7dec00c26c28dd78102e3ed9d0f3/docs/iam/password-permissions.md).\n\nThe maintained integration target is `pgsty/silo`; upstream MinIO compatibility remains best effort.\n\n[Full changes](https://github.com/pgsty/mc/compare/RELEASE.2026-09-03T07-13-05Z...RELEASE.2026-09-13T00-00-00Z)\n\n## Component status — 2026-09-13\n\npkg v3.14.0 and mcli 20260913 are published. Matching password-permission handling is merged in Server and Console, but their latest public releases remain Server 20260903 and Console v2.4.0 and do not contain that split. Installing the client alone does not change server-side authorization. Retain both CreateUser and ChangeMyPassword denies wherever the old combined restriction must survive an upgrade or rollback.\n\nSee the [current component matrix](https://silo.pgsty.com/compatibility/versions/), [password-policy migration](https://silo.pgsty.com/compatibility/password-permissions/) and [website release notes](https://silo.pgsty.com/blog/release/mcli-20260913/).\n"
